  abstract = {In this chapter, we discuss the Middle-Out Engagement Framework, which focuses on two cases undertaken in countries with emerging economies and their potential to inform broader practices of collaborative city-making. The cases discuss top-down and bottom-up collaborations that work toward acknowledging the importance of putting people back into the ``smart.'' In each case, we explore how creativity and technology can play a critical role in assisting the development and communication of ideas and knowledge sharing. Our focus on emerging countries highlights the influence that place and culture have on city-making initiatives, enabling us to propose a robust framework for the design, development, and deployment of middle-out engagement approaches across various urban contexts and scales.}
