  abstract = {The completion of initiatives designed to address wicked problems often requires the participation of a variety of actors spanning multiple generations of both individuals and organizations. Until now, frameworks for addressing problems and articulating the sustainability of goals related to overcoming them have yet to adequately account for the timespans required for addressing such problems; particularly as far as the lifecycle of organizations is shorter than such timespans. Here, a framework is presented to articulate the survival of goals to the point of initiative completion under conditions in which it is not assumed that any individual organization or subunit exists long enough to fulfill the requirements for completing such initiatives.}
